      "label": "Text 71",
      "config": {
        "text": "<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1.125rem;\">This interactive map provides an at-a-glance view of current fire restrictions across Larimer County, divided into three elevation zones: below 6,000 feet, 6,000–9,000 feet, and above 9,000 feet. The map reflects county, private, and state land status to help you plan responsibly. </strong></p><p style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1.125rem;\">Please note: fire restrictions for federal lands and municipalities—like Rocky Mountain National Park and U.S. Forest Service areas—are not shown. For those areas, </span><a href=\"layout_0_block_51\" target=\"_self\" data-uniqueid=\"86829695_bceb_cba8_2276_3381cf6aedea\" data-dsid=\"\" data-link=\"%7B%22linkType%22%3A%22BLOCK%22%2C%22value%22%3A%22layout_0_block_51%22%7D\" style=\"font-size: 1.125rem;\">visit the respective agency’s website.</a></p>",
        "style": {
          "wrap": true
        }
